#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""Browse, search, resume and fork the sessions of the claude, codex and
opencode CLIs.

Everything a listing shows - title, first prompt, directory, the first and the
last message - and every message of a session are kept in an SQLite index in
the cache folder. A session file is only read where it grew since it was last
looked at, and then only from the byte where the last look stopped, so a
session of a hundred megabytes that got one more message costs that message.
The messages are in a full-text table as well, which is what makes a search
over all of them answer at once instead of grepping gigabytes of tool output.
"""

